This code uses the pigpio library to interface with the Raspberry Pi's GPIO and I2C buses. It initializes the ADS1115 ADC bridge, configures it to read from AIN0 and AIN1, and reads the pressure and temperature values from the bridge. It then converts these values to pressure and temperature using linear transfer functions and displays them on the console. The code also drives a warning LED on GPIO17 HIGH when the pressure exceeds 105.0 kPa. The code handles errors by retrying failed I2C reads up to 3 times and by releasing resources on SIGINT.

