This code uses the pigpio library to interact with the Raspberry Pi's GPIO and SPI interfaces. It reads the current from the Melexis MLX91209 Hall-effect current sensor using the MCP3008 10-bit SPI ADC, converts the reading to a voltage and then to a current, and logs the result to a file. If the current exceeds 10A, it asserts the GPIO shutdown pin and logs an OVERCURRENT event. The program also handles errors and cleans up resources on exit. The signal handler is registered to catch SIGINT and SIGTERM signals and perform a clean shutdown.

