This code reads data from the Si1172-A30-GMR Optical Heart Rate Sensor using the pigpio library and logs it to a CSV file named `biometric_log.csv`. It handles SIGINT (Ctrl+C) by closing the I2C handle, terminating pigpio, and closing the log file. The code also checks the return value of every pigpio I2C call and logs an error row with the appropriate error flag when a read fails. The Si1172's command-based register access protocol is used to trigger a measurement and read the FIFO or data registers. The raw 16-bit IR and RED ADC values are logged as proxy values for HR and SpO2 respectively, with a comment documenting this limitation.

