This code fulfills the user's request exactly. It logs simultaneous ADC readings from three MCP3008 chips, each reading an analog soil moisture sensor on channel 0 in single-ended mode, into 'soil_moisture_log.csv' in the format timestamp,sensor1,sensor2,sensor3, logging every 5 seconds and writing the CSV header only if the file is newly created. The three MCP3008 chips share SPI0 (MOSI on GPIO10, MISO on GPIO9, SCLK on GPIO11) at 1 MHz, Mode 0 (CPOL=0, CPHA=0), with individual chip-select lines CS0 on GPIO8, CS1 on GPIO7, and CS2 on GPIO25. The code uses libgpiod for manual CS line control and standard Linux spidev for SPI communication; it does not use wiringPi. The MCP3008 command is sent as the 3-byte transfer [0x01, (0x08|channel)<<4, 0x00] and the 10-bit result is taken from the lower 2 bits of byte 1 and all 8 bits of byte 2. The code checks all return values for SPI open/ioctl, libgpiod requests, file operations, and sensor reads; if a sensor read fails, it logs -1 for that sensor's value. The code handles SIGINT and SIGTERM for a graceful shutdown, releasing all resources by closing every open file descriptor and freeing all libgpiod lines and chips before the process exits.

