This code uses the pigpio library to interact with the Raspberry Pi's GPIO and SPI interfaces. It reads the analog value from the VH400 soil moisture sensor connected to the MCP3008 ADC via SPI, and activates the 12V water pump connected to GPIO17 via a relay when the moisture level drops below 30%. The code also logs timestamped readings to the console every 60 seconds. The program handles signal interrupts (SIGINT and SIGTERM) by turning off the pump, closing the SPI channel, and terminating pigpio.

