This code uses the pigpio library to control two Adafruit Mini DC Motors with wires on a Raspberry Pi 4 Model B. It reads the speed of each motor from a potentiometer via an MCP3008 ADC over SPI, maps the 10-bit potentiometer values to speed factors using a logarithmic function, and runs a motion profile that moves the motors forward and backward simultaneously or sequentially with a short delay. The code includes robust error handling for all pigpio and SPI operations and releases all resources on exit, including via signal handlers for SIGINT and SIGTERM.

