This code uses the libgpiod library to control the GPIO pins on the Raspberry Pi 4 Model B. It reads the digital output of the KY-038 sound sensor module connected to GPIO17 and triggers a simulated alarm LED on GPIO18 when sound is detected. The program prints the sound level reading to the console each loop iteration and blinks the alarm LED for 1 second when sound is detected. The program also handles signal interrupts (Ctrl+C or SIGTERM) by releasing all GPIO lines and exiting cleanly.

