This code captures MJPEG video from a USB webcam connected at `/dev/video0` and logs the timestamp of each captured frame to a file named `frame_log.txt`. The video capture is configured for a resolution of 640x480. The program uses memory-mapped buffers for frame capture and handles input and output asynchronously with `select()` to prevent blocking indefinitely. The code includes robust error handling for every V4L2 ioctl call, every file operation, and every memory mapping. It also ensures clean resource release on all exit paths, including a graceful shutdown triggered by SIGINT.

