This code uses the `pigpio` library to initialize the GPIO and configure it as an input with a pull-down resistor. It then enters a loop where it polls the GPIO every 100 ms, checking for motion. If motion is detected, it captures a JPEG image using the `libcamera-still` command and sends it to the specified server using `libcurl`. The server IP and port are passed as command-line arguments. The program handles errors and exits cleanly on SIGINT and SIGTERM signals.

