This code uses the pigpio library to interact with the Raspberry Pi's GPIO, I2C, and SPI buses. It displays the wind speed and direction on a 16x2 LCD connected to the I2C bus, and updates the display every 500 ms. The wind speed is calculated by counting the number of pulses on GPIO17 and multiplying it by 0.5 m/s per pulse. The wind direction is read from an MCP3008 ADC connected to the SPI bus, and is linearly mapped to a value between 0 and 359 degrees. The code also handles SIGINT and SIGTERM signals to ensure that all resources are released when the program exits.

