This code uses the pigpio library to interface with the VL53L1X time-of-flight sensor and control a small DC motor based on the measured distance. The sensor is connected to the I2C bus 1 at its default address 0x29. The motor is connected to GPIO17 (forward) and GPIO18 (backward). The code uses a rising edge interrupt on GPIO24 to trigger a distance reading and control the motor accordingly. The distance threshold for forward and backward movement is set to 100 mm and 300 mm, respectively. The code also includes error handling for I2C transactions and GPIO operations. The motor is stopped safely when the program exits due to a SIGINT or SIGTERM signal.

