This code uses the standard Linux I2C ioctl calls to interface with the Si1182-A-GM optical sensor. It initializes the sensor by verifying the part ID register and configuring the measurement rate register. It then enters a loop where it reads the ambient light and proximity data from the sensor every 100 ms, converts the ambient light to lux, and logs the timestamped reading to a file and prints it to stdout. The code also handles I2C bus errors, sensor absence, and SIGINT and SIGTERM signals to ensure all resources are released on every exit path.

