This code uses the `pigpio` library to interact with the Raspberry Pi's GPIO pins. It sets up GPIO17 as an output, GPIO18 as an input with a falling/rising edge alert callback, and GPIO27 as an output. It generates a 10 us trigger pulse on GPIO17, then measures the echo pulse width using the interrupt callback function. The distance is calculated as round-trip time * 0.0343 / 2 and printed to stdout every second. If the distance is below 20 cm, the buzzer pin is set high, otherwise it is set low. The program handles SIGINT (Ctrl+C) by terminating pigpio and exiting with proper resource cleanup.

