This code uses the `pigpio` library to interact with the I2C bus and the `sht40_crc8` function to calculate the CRC-8 checksum. It reads the temperature and humidity from the SHT40 sensor, validates the CRC-8 checksums, and prints the readings to the console every 5 seconds. If an I2C read/write error or CRC failure occurs, it prints a diagnostic message to stderr and re-opens the I2C bus before the next attempt. The program also handles SIGINT and SIGTERM signals for a graceful shutdown, closing the I2C handle and terminating `pigpio` on exit.

