This code uses the pigpio library to interface with the Sensirion SCD40 CO2 sensor over I2C bus 1 at address 0x62. It initializes the pigpio library and opens the I2C bus with error checking. It sends the start-periodic-measurement command 0x21B1 and waits at least 1 second before reading. Every 5 seconds in the main loop, it reads CO2, temperature, and humidity with command 0xE000, which returns 9 bytes as three 2-byte-plus-CRC values; validates the CRC-8 (polynomial 0x31, initial value 0xFF) for each, and if a CRC check or I2C transaction fails, logs the error and skips that reading. It converts the values with CO2 in ppm, temperature = -45 + 175 * raw / 65535, and humidity = 100 * raw / 65535. It stores each valid reading (timestamp, CO2, temperature, humidity) in a thread-safe circular buffer of capacity 100. It spawns a separate thread that every 60 seconds writes the entire buffer to a timestamped CSV file, with a header row, in /var/log/scd40_data/ (creating the directory if needed). It uses a volatile sig_atomic_t running flag and handles SIGINT gracefully: stops the main loop, sends the stop-periodic-measurement command 0x3F86, joins the logging thread, flushes any remaining buffer data to a final CSV file, closes the I2C handle, and terminates pigpio. It logs all errors with timestamps to /var/log/scd40_error.log, ensuring no resource leaks on any exit path.

