This code uses the pigpio library to sample the BMP180 pressure sensor over I2C bus 1 at address 0x77 every 50 ms, using a pigpio hardware timer. It reads the 11 calibration coefficients from the sensor and uses them to calculate the pressure. The pressure readings are logged to a circular buffer sized for 60 seconds of data, and an alert is triggered if the current pressure deviates by more than 5 hPa from the rolling average of the last 60 seconds. The alert is logged to stderr and the GPIO24 pin is set high. The code also handles I2C failures and sensor absence, and logs errors to stderr. The resources are released on SIGINT by closing the I2C handle, resetting GPIO, and terminating pigpio.

