This code uses the `pigpio` library to interact with the Raspberry Pi's GPIO pins. It initializes the library, sets up GPIO 4 as an input with an internal pull-up resistor, and polls the pin every 50 ms. When an obstacle is detected (i.e., the pin reads 0), it records the timestamp and reading in a circular buffer and prints an alert to stdout. On SIGINT (Ctrl+C), it prints the buffer contents in chronological order, releases all `pigpio` resources, and exits cleanly.

