This code uses the libgpiod v1.x API to read the 8 individual touch states from a TTP226 8-channel capacitive touch sensor connected to BCM GPIO pins 5, 6, 13, 19, 26, 12, 16, and 20. It polls all eight pins every 50 milliseconds, logging only state changes (touch detected / released) to the console with ISO-8601 timestamps and the sensor index plus BCM pin number. The code handles errors for GPIO chip initialization, line resolution, bulk line requests, and read failures, printing a descriptive error (including errno) and exiting with a non-zero status on unrecoverable failures. It also ensures clean resource release on all exit paths, including graceful shutdown on SIGINT (Ctrl+C).

