This code uses the pigpio library to control the VEML7700 lux sensor and an LED on the Raspberry Pi 4 Model B. It reads the ALS register of the sensor once per second, converts the value to lux, and controls the LED brightness based on the lux value. The brightness is calculated using an adaptive logic that adjusts the brightness based on the lux value. The code also logs each sample to a file named 'grow_log.txt' with an ISO timestamp, lux value, brightness, and error code. The code checks for errors during initialization, I2C operations, and PWM operations, and logs and handles sensor-absent/bus-error paths. On SIGINT/SIGTERM, the code turns off the LED, closes the log file, closes the I2C bus, and terminates pigpio.

