This code uses the libgpiod library to monitor a Keyes KY-026 flame sensor connected to GPIO17 on a Raspberry Pi 3 Model B+. It configures the line as an input with an internal pull-up and polls it every 100 ms. When a falling edge is detected, it prints 'FLAME DETECTED' to the console and appends a line with the current timestamp and 'FLAME DETECTED' to 'flame_log.txt' in append mode. The code also installs a SIGINT/SIGTERM handler for graceful shutdown that releases the GPIO line, closes the chip, and closes the log file on all exit paths.

