This code uses the libgpiod C library to read a 3-Way Tracking Sensor connected to Broadcom GPIO pins 2, 3, and 4 on a Raspberry Pi 3 Model B+. It polls the sensor lines every 100 ms and logs the values to stdout in the format 'L:<0|1> M:<0|1> R:<0|1>'. The code checks every libgpiod call and handles the case where the gpiochip device is absent or permission-denied. It also uses signal handling for SIGINT (Ctrl+C) to terminate gracefully and release resources.

