```

This code uses the pigpio library to control a common-anode RGB LED connected to GPIO17 (Red), GPIO18 (Green), and GPIO27 (Blue) on a Raspberry Pi 4 Model B. It smoothly fades between randomly chosen hues every 5 seconds using hardware PWM at 1000 Hz with an 8-bit (0-255) range, applying a 50-step linear interpolation over each 5-second fade. The LED is common-anode, so the PWM duty-cycle values are inverted by taking the complement of each value. The code also handles SIGINT and SIGTERM signals for graceful shutdown by turning off the LED, releasing pigpio resources, and closing syslog.

