This code uses the `gpiod` library to interface with the GPIO pins on the Raspberry Pi 5. It performs a self-test by blinking the LED twice and reading the flame sensor five times at 100 ms intervals. If the sensor consistently reads LOW, it treats it as a sensor fault and signals the error with a distinct pattern. After the self-test, it polls the flame sensor every 50 ms in the main loop and activates the buzzer and LED when flame is detected. It logs all events with timestamps and cleans up all GPIO lines on normal exit and on SIGINT.

