This code uses the `pigpio` library to interface with the Raspberry Pi's GPIO and I2C buses. It initializes the ADXL345 accelerometer, configures it for full-resolution mode at the +-2g range, and polls the sensor every 10 ms to detect sudden impacts. If the total acceleration magnitude exceeds 2.5g, it turns on a red LED connected to GPIO17 for 500 ms and appends a timestamped entry containing the magnitude and X/Y/Z components to "impact_log.txt". The code also handles sensor-absent and bus-error paths, and ensures clean resource release of the I2C handle, LED, log file, and `pigpio` on all exit paths including SIGINT/SIGTERM.

