This code uses the standard Linux `/dev/i2c-1` ioctl interface to interact with the I2C bus. It opens the bus, writes the One-Time High-Resolution Mode 2 command to the BH1750FVI sensor, waits for the maximum conversion time, reads 2 bytes of data, calculates the illuminance in lux, and logs the reading to a file named `light_log.txt`. The program continuously logs readings every 5 seconds until interrupted by a SIGINT signal (Ctrl+C). It handles potential I2C write/read errors and sensor-absent paths, and releases resources on all exit paths.

