This code uses the libgpiod library to control the GPIO pins on the Raspberry Pi 3 Model B+. It sets up two GPIO lines as outputs, sets them to low, and then enters a loop where it alternates between energizing solenoid 1 and solenoid 2 for 500 ms each. The loop continues until an error occurs or the program is interrupted with Ctrl+C. The signal handler is installed to clean up and exit cleanly when the program is interrupted.

