This code uses the `pigpio` library to control the GPIO pins on the Raspberry Pi. It sets up the TTP223 capacitive touch sensor on GPIO4 to trigger a callback function when touched, which toggles the relay on GPIO17 and appends a JSON object to a log file. The relay is initially set to OFF, and on SIGINT, it turns the relay OFF and appends a final OFF entry to the log before exiting cleanly. The code also debounces touches in software with a minimum 200 ms gap between registered touches.

