This code uses the Linux I2C-dev interface to communicate with the MPU-6050 gyroscope. It opens the I2C bus, writes to the PWR_MGMT_1 register to wake the sensor, and then enters a loop where it reads the 6 bytes of gyroscope data, converts the raw values to degrees/second, and logs the timestamped readings to a file. The loop runs at 10 Hz and exits when a SIGINT or SIGTERM signal is received. The file descriptors are closed on exit.

