This code will create a traffic light simulation using four 5V relay modules connected to GPIO17, GPIO22, GPIO23, and GPIO24 on a Raspberry Pi 4 Model B. The relays are active-low, meaning that setting a line to 0 turns the relay on and setting it to 1 turns it off. The program will cycle through the states red, red+yellow, green, and yellow, then repeat indefinitely. The program will exit cleanly when interrupted by a SIGINT or SIGTERM signal.

