This code uses the `libgpiod` library to interact with the GPIO pins on the Raspberry Pi Zero W. It monitors the KY-026 flame sensor on GPIO17 and activates a buzzer on GPIO18 and an LED on GPIO23 when flame is detected. The sensor reading is debounced with three consecutive reads at 50 ms intervals. The program logs each flame-detection event with a timestamp and the message 'Flame Detected' to `flame_log.txt`. The program handles errors for all GPIO operations and releases all resources on any error exit path. It also handles SIGINT and SIGTERM signals for graceful cleanup by releasing the GPIO lines and closing the log file.

