This code uses the pigpio library to control a 5V relay connected to GPIO17 (physical pin 11) using a TTP223 capacitive touch sensor connected to GPIO4 (physical pin 7). The relay is active-high, so it is energized when GPIO17 is HIGH. The TTP223 outputs logic HIGH when touched, and an external pull-down resistor is assumed to be connected to GPIO4. The program debounces each touch with a delay of at least 50 ms after detection. It checks every pigpio initialisation call and GPIO operation, handling sensor-absent or bus-error conditions gracefully, and ensures clean resource release on all exit paths, including SIGINT/SIGTERM signal handling. The program runs indefinitely until terminated by Ctrl+C.

