```

This code uses the pigpio library to read acceleration data from an Adafruit LIS3DH accelerometer over I2C bus 1 at address 0x18. It implements a basic fall detection system that triggers a buzzer on GPIO17 when the acceleration magnitude drops below the freefall threshold and exceeds the impact threshold. The code initializes pigpio and I2C with error checking, configures the LIS3DH for a 100 Hz data rate and ±2g full scale, and continuously reads 16-bit signed acceleration values starting from register OUT_X_L (0x28). The code also handles I2C communication failures with up to 3 retries and performs graceful cleanup on SIGINT.

