This code implements a smart chicken coop lighting system using the pigpio library on a Raspberry Pi 4 Model B. It controls a 12V relay-connected LED strip via GPIO 17 (active-high) based on ambient light read from a BH1750 sensor on I2C bus 1 at address 0x23. The relay activates at dusk, when lux falls below 50, and deactivates at dawn, when lux exceeds 200, using a hysteresis loop to prevent rapid toggling. It polls the sensor every 5 seconds, waiting at least 180 ms after issuing the One-Time High-Resolution Mode 2 command (0x21) before reading the 2 bytes of lux data, and converts the raw data to lux by dividing by 1.2. It logs all sensor readings and relay state changes to chicken_coop_log.txt in the format 'YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS: Lux = XXX, Relay = ON/OFF'. It implements comprehensive error handling for pigpio initialization, I2C bus communication, and file I/O; if the sensor fails to respond, it logs the error and safely turns off the relay. It ensures clean resource release of the I2C handle, the relay GPIO, and the log file on all exit paths, including graceful shutdown via SIGINT and SIGTERM.

