This code uses the pigpio library to control the GPIO pins, the HX711 load cell amplifier, and the servo motor. It also uses the json-c library to generate JSON objects for logging. The code reads the calibration factor, server IP, and server port from a config.ini file, and falls back to default values if the file is missing or malformed. The code also uses signal handlers to clean up resources on exit.

Please note that this code assumes that the HX711 load cell amplifier is connected to GPIO 23 (DATA) and GPIO 24 (SCK), and the servo motor is connected to GPIO 18. You may need to adjust these pin numbers to match your specific setup.

Also, this code uses a simple timeout of 1000 attempts to read the load cell data. You may need to adjust this timeout value depending on your specific setup.

Finally, this code assumes that the config.ini file is in the same directory as the executable. You may need to adjust the file path to match your specific setup.

