This code uses the pigpio library to control a servo motor on GPIO18 and two push buttons on GPIO21 and GPIO22. The lock button is connected to an internal pull-up, and the unlock button is connected to an internal pull-up. When the lock button is pressed, the servo moves to the locked position with a pulse width of 1000 microseconds. When the unlock button is pressed, the servo moves to the unlocked position with a pulse width of 2000 microseconds. The servo pulse width is limited to the safe range of 500-2500 microseconds at all times. The code also debounces each button press with a 100 ms delay. The SIGINT signal handler is set up to release all resources on exit.

