This code uses the pigpio library to decode NEC IR remote signals from an IR receiver connected to GPIO17 (BCM) on a Raspberry Pi 3 Model B+. It registers a pigpio alert callback to capture pulse timings, decodes the 32-bit NEC frame using its 9 ms mark plus 4.5 ms space header, 560 microsecond bit marks, and 1690 microsecond spaces, validates the decoded command against its inverted copy, and logs the decoded address and command to syslog. It also publishes each decoded command as JSON to an MQTT broker at localhost:1883 on topic ir/decoded using the paho-mqtt v2 callback semantics. The code checks pigpio initialization, handles GPIO initialization failures, guards against pulse buffer overflow, validates the NEC checksum, and cleanly releases pigpio, MQTT, and syslog resources on SIGINT or SIGTERM.

